From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duelists Kingdom Engine <engine@duelistskingdom.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the declared opponent of a lock after its activator
 leaves

At n > 2 the event filter of effect::is_activateable (patch 0072) compared the subject of a draw,
summon or battle event with the declared opponent of a bound field effect. It used
field::event_opponent(registered_player, e), which names nobody when registered_player left the
duel (patch 0044 guard). The filter was skipped, so a resolved lock such as Eradicator Epidemic Virus
hit every opponent after its activator surrendered. When the registering seat is not alive, the
filter now reads the subject of the event (or the battle opponent) directly. Rulebook v1.4,
Removing players from the game: the declared opponent still has to destroy cards until the end of
their third turn. event_opponent keeps its dead-seat guard for its other callers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019EpX1AcvnigK9dTsxAa5W9

---
diff --git a/effect.cpp b/effect.cpp
index c118e31..93d8edc 100644
--- a/effect.cpp
+++ b/effect.cpp
@@ -157,7 +157,16 @@ int32_t effect::is_activateable(uint8_t playerid, const tevent& e, int32_t negle
 	// A draw, summon or battle response stays with its saved subject. Leaving the field can have a different reason player.
 	if(has_bound_opponent() && !s_range && !o_range
 		&& (field::event_player_is_subject(e.event_code) || field::event_is_battle(e.event_code))) {
-		const uint8_t event_opp = pduel->game_field->event_opponent(registered_player, e);
+		auto& gf = *pduel->game_field;
+		uint8_t event_opp = gf.event_opponent(registered_player, e);
+		// event_opponent names nobody for a seat that left. A resolved lock of that seat (Eradicator) still binds
+		// its declared opponent, so compare the subject of the event with that opponent directly.
+		if(event_opp == DUELIST_NONE && gf.n_duelists > 2 && gf.is_duelist(registered_player) && !gf.is_alive(registered_player)) {
+			if(field::event_is_battle(e.event_code))
+				event_opp = gf.battle_opponent(registered_player);
+			else if(gf.is_alive(e.event_player) && !gf.same_team(registered_player, e.event_player))
+				event_opp = e.event_player;
+		}
 		if(event_opp != DUELIST_NONE && event_opp != registered_opp)
 			return FALSE;
 	}
